HST Office: menu items show LibreOffice's own icons in every HST icon style.

Reason: owner decision of 20/11/2026. Menu icons (context menus, menu bar, drop-down menus) reuse the
LibreOffice (Colibre) icons at their right size, so they stay as sharp as upstream; the HST glyphs
stay on the ribbon and the frame. Until now a menu took the command's icon from the current style:
the Cổ điển style forced its Find and Replace glyphs into the menus (they replace Colibre's on the
ribbon), and the Hiện đại style put an HST glyph on every command it draws.
MenuBarManager::FillMenuImages now asks vcl::CommandInfoProvider::GetMenuImageForCommand, which loads
"cmd/sc_<command>.png" from colibre_svg / colibre_dark_svg when the current style is an HST one, at the
display's icon scale (so the 150 % rule of hst-icon-theme-fractional-scale.patch applies), and falls back
to GetImageForCommand for commands Colibre does not draw (the HST extension's), commands with arguments
and every non-HST theme. Known limit: an icon a user assigned to a command in Tools > Customize is not
shown in menus for commands Colibre draws.

Applies after hst-icon-theme-fractional-scale.patch.
Test: make CppunitTest_vcl_app_test (test_HstIconTheme: MenusUseLibreOfficeIcons).
License: upstream files remain MPL-2.0.
